L669: ## cite19†`rebase-strategy` L670: 
L671: Disable automatic rebasing of pull requests raised by Dependabot.
L672: 
L673: Dependabot default behavior is to rebase open pull requests when Dependabot detects any changes to a version or security update pull request. Dependabot checks for changes when:
L674:   * Your schedule runs to check for version updates.
L675:   * You reopen a closed Dependabot pull request.
L676:   * You change the value of `target-branch` in the Dependabot configuration file, see cite22†`target-branch` .
L677:   * A Dependabot pull request is in conflict after a recent push to the target branch.
L678: 
L679: When `rebase-strategy` is set to `disabled`, Dependabot stops rebasing pull requests.
L680: 
L681: Note
L682: Pull requests that were open before you disable rebasing will continue to be rebased until 30 days after they were opened. This affects all pull requests that have conflicts with the target branch and all pull requests for version updates.
L683: ## cite20†`registries` L684: 
L685: Configure access to private package registries to allow Dependabot to update a wider range of dependencies, see cite66†Configuring access to private registries for Dependabot and cite67†Guidance for the configuration of private registries for Dependabot .
