58: // BenchmarkNeutralGraphCapability states what Graph can do without telling the agent
59: // what to do first. It exists so an A/B harness that must avoid arm-asymmetric
60: // instructions has somewhere to take its wording FROM, instead of editing the guides
61: // below. It is never part of GraphGuide, CombinedGuide, or BrainGuide. It names
62: // --format agent for the cost reason above, not as an instruction: a capability
63: // statement may say how the tool is invoked without telling an arm what to do.
64: const BenchmarkNeutralGraphCapability = `Graph answers code-discovery, structural, and semantic-change questions:
65: 
66:     entire graph query --repo . --profile full --format agent --query "<task>"
67: 
68: query, def, neighbors, and impact locate code and report structure. diff, commit, and
69: checkpoint compare revisions. Graph interactive queries normally inspect the working
70: tree; --head selects committed source. Static relations can be incomplete.
